# Document Conventions

## Where things go

| Folder | Content |
|--------|---------|
| `docs/context/` | Stable background: agency profile, process map, evaluation framework |
| `ideas/` | Ideas at any stage, one file each |
| `research/` | Findings on tools, vendors, technologies, markets, regulations |
| `processes/` | Deep dives on a business process, written for an archetype |
| `templates/` | Starting points for the above. Copy, don't edit in place |

## File naming

- Lowercase kebab-case: `appointment-no-show-reduction.md`.
- No dates in filenames. Put dates in the frontmatter.
- One topic per file. Split when a file covers two distinct things.

## Frontmatter

Ideas, research and process docs start with:

```yaml
---
title: Human readable title
status: seed | exploring | validated | parked | rejected
created: YYYY-MM-DD
updated: YYYY-MM-DD
process: acquisition | booking | delivery | comms-support | payments | retention | reputation | operations | admin-finance | cross-cutting
---
```

Update `status` and `updated` whenever the thinking changes materially.

## Style

- Plain, concise language. Lead with the conclusion, then the reasoning.
- Link related docs with relative links.
- Keep assumptions and open questions in their own sections.
- Remember `client-agnostic.mdc`: no real client details.
